From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 10:41:08 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] virgl: reach an imported host blob with copy transfers

A texture imported from a HOST3D blob has no guest pages this driver
could map. The kernel makes a blob without VIRTGPU_BLOB_FLAG_USE_MAPPABLE
a VRAM object and refuses to mmap it, and minigbm makes exactly those of
every buffer a guest never reads or writes itself: window buffers,
hardware bitmaps and EGL images on Android. The import turned staging on
only when the layout was larger than the guest storage, which for a blob
is its whole host size, so a map of the texture took the resource itself,
failed, and returned NULL. A write map was then dropped without a word by
u_default_texture_subdata, losing the upload, and a read map became
GL_OUT_OF_MEMORY with the caller left holding stale memory.

Import such a blob with use_staging whenever the host can copy-transfer in
both directions. Uploads then go through WRITE_TO_STAGING and reads
through READ_FROM_STAGING, the paths a resource uses once it outgrows its
guest storage. A host that cannot keeps the previous behaviour.

The choice is made at import because RESOURCE_INFO does not report a
blob's flags, so a mappable HOST3D blob takes the copy path too. None is
imported into GL today, since gralloc never sets MAPPABLE for GPU-only
use; one that appears should fall back to staging only after
resource_map fails.

A read needs the renderer to accept a copy transfer from a blob texture.
Without that, it returns zeros where it used to raise GL_OUT_OF_MEMORY.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_resource.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_resource.c b/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_resource.c
index 9a163ff9c73a3dc7afd26793cc013d2d4a643cb2..64de0f7df42f954df56c423603ad534c3ccb8edc 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_resource.c
@@ -871,6 +871,14 @@ static struct pipe_resource *virgl_resource_from_handle(struct pipe_screen *scre
    if (res->metadata.total_size > storage_size)
       res->use_staging = 1;
 
+   /* A HOST3D blob has no guest storage this driver could map: its pages
+    * belong to the renderer, and a GPU-only one is not even mappable through
+    * the kernel. Reach it with copy transfers, as a resource whose layout
+    * outgrows its guest storage does.
+    */
+   if (res->blob_mem == VIRGL_BLOB_MEM_HOST3D && virgl_can_use_staging(vs, res))
+      res->use_staging = 1;
+
    /* assign blob resource a type in case it was created untyped */
    if (res->blob_mem && plane == 0 &&
        (vs->caps.caps.v2.host_feature_check_version >= 18 ||
